      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Excessive bleeding post coronary artery bypass surgery (CABG) remains a major source of morbidity and mortality. Approaching this bleeding with a resternotomy, while necessary in the vast majority of cases, is associated with an increased incidence of infections and sternal wound complications. A thoracoscopic approach in select patients with a pleural based collection is described."},
